+    "id": "mosh-dqw.10",
+    "title": "Remote attach path: attacher, dispatch and status capability hooks",
+    "description": "Remote attach path (R1, R12, R16): attacher that validates the private rendezvous dir, finds or spawns the keeper, checks the keeper's peer uid, pumps stdio (and reports its own bring-up failure as END{keeper-unavailable}), the --x-mosh-* dispatch, host.rs hooks, and the status capability advertisement.\nSpec: docs/superpowers/runs/2026-10-24-mosh-phase1-resumable-session/2026-10-24-mosh-phase1-resumable-session-design.md (§Keeper 'Rendezvous', 'Attacher failure reporting' and 'Spawn', §Upstream touch list host.rs/status.rs rows, §Key abstractions Attacher/remote::dispatch).\nsrc/mosh/remote/{mod,attacher}.rs. remote::dispatch: closed match routing --x-mosh-session-v1 to the attacher and --x-mosh-keeper-v1 to the keeper entry point (keeper::run, filled by mosh-dqw.7; the arm calls it by name). Attacher, per the rendezvous contract defined by the scaffold in mosh::remote (mosh-dqw.1): validate the private dir (directory, not symlink, euid-owned, mode 0700), connect to the keeper socket path and, after every successful connect, verify the peer uid (SO_PEERCRED on Linux, getpeereid on macOS, via libc) equals its own euid before forwarding a single byte; on ENOENT/ECONNREFUSED take the spawn lock, retry connect, then try the live lock non-blocking: acquired ⇒ no keeper alive: unlink the stale socket, release the live lock and spawn the keeper; not acquired ⇒ a keeper is alive but not listening yet: retry connect up to 5 s, then re-try the live lock once (if acquired, continue as in the first branch). Spawn: current_exe [--session S] remote-client-bridge --x-mosh-keeper-v1 via detach_server_daemon_command (setsid) plus a plain spawn (not the launchd path), env_remove(SSH_AUTH_SOCK) and Stdio::null() on stdin, stdout and stderr (so the keeper holds none of the sshd channel fds and its output can never reach the leg); wait ≤5 s for the socket, connect; release the spawn lock; then pump with crate::platform::forward_remote_bridge_stdio(keeper_stream, false) unchanged. Any bring-up failure (dir validation, lock or spawn error, 5 s wait, peer-uid mismatch): write exactly one session END{\"keeper-unavailable\"} on stdout (encoded with the session codec) and exit non-zero; this is the only message the attacher originates, once connected it is a pure byte pipe. Upstream hooks: host.rs match arm `[o, ..] if o.starts_with(\"--x-mosh-\") =\u003e false, // mosh-fork hook`; host.rs `if let Some(result) = super::attach::mosh::remote::dispatch(args) { return result; } // mosh-fork hook` after the ssh-agent registration; status.rs pushes \"x-mosh-resume-bridge-v1\" into endpoint_capabilities on Unix (a fork test asserts it equals mosh::STATUS_CAPABILITY).\nowns: Attacher (fills attacher::run); owns: remote::dispatch; owns: the status.rs hook that emits STATUS_CAPABILITY (string and placement owned by mosh-dqw.1); owns: attacher END{keeper-unavailable} reporting and peer-uid check\nconsumes: mosh constants and MoshConfig\nconsumes: keeper and attacher entry-point signatures; consumes: keeper rendezvous protocol (private dir and owner checks, socket path, live lock, spawn lock); consumes: mosh module tree; consumes: SessionMsg\nconsumes: rendezvous pure-pipe rule (attacher writes nothing but END{keeper-unavailable})\nblocked-by mosh-dqw.1: consumes keeper rendezvous protocol and mosh module tree\nblocked-by mosh-dqw.4: consumes SessionMsg (END{keeper-unavailable} encoding)\nFiles: src/mosh/remote/mod.rs, src/mosh/remote/attacher.rs, src/remote/host.rs (2 hook lines), src/cli/status.rs (1 hook line)\nAcceptance:\n- [ ] Exactly 3 upstream lines changed, tagged; existing remote_attach tests pass; an unknown --x-mosh-* flag is an error, not silently accepted as plain.\n- [ ] In-process tests: stale socket file with no listener is recovered (unlinked, keeper spawn path taken); two concurrent attachers spawn at most one keeper (lock); a live keeper is connected to without spawning; live lock held but socket not yet listening retries connect then re-tries the lock.\n- [ ] A foreign-owned, symlinked or wrong-mode private dir, and a peer-uid mismatch, each yield exactly one END{\"keeper-unavailable\"} on stdout and a non-zero exit, before any byte is forwarded; the keeper spawn command has null stdin/stdout/stderr, env_remove(SSH_AUTH_SOCK) and setsid.\n- [ ] status client --json includes x-mosh-resume-bridge-v1 on Unix.",
