+    "id": "mosh-dqw.8",
+    "title": "Local bridge: resumable client pump and start_ui_bridge resume path",
+    "description": "Local bridge (R1-R7, R9, R10, R12): per-client resumable pump (leg I/O thread plus a separate client-writer thread, pre-WELCOME read gate) that keeps the client stream whole, buffers input through outages, injects status frames that keep saved-machine health alive and drive the banner, enforces the give-up deadline, delivers server-EOF frames then closes, and takes the plain path for kill switch, Windows or non-Unix-local builds, or no capability.\nSpec: docs/superpowers/runs/2026-10-24-mosh-phase1-resumable-session/2026-10-24-mosh-phase1-resumable-session-design.md (§Local bridge behaviour, §Discovery and fallback step 4, §Session-end triggers, §Error handling summary, §Key abstractions LocalBridge/start_ui_bridge).\nsrc/mosh/local_bridge.rs plus the resume branch of start_ui_bridge in src/mosh/mod.rs. LocalBridge binds the user-facing socket with crate::ipc prepare_socket_path/bind_private_local_listener/restrict_socket_permissions (as start_command does at attach.rs:3038-3051) and serves one connection at a time. Ghost eviction: the last session token is kept in a process-global map in local_bridge.rs keyed by the bridge's local socket path (the local_socket argument of start_ui_bridge), not per bridge instance, so it survives a saved machine's reconnects that build a new bridge (saved.rs:20-55, supervisor.rs:477); a new connection's HELLO carries it as previous_token. Per connection: SessionEndpoint (8 MiB outbound ring, 256 KiB window while a leg is up), dial legs through the LegDialer; threads: a leg I/O thread (session messages, timers, should_stop polled every \u003c=100 ms, never blocks on the network or the client socket) and a client-writer thread owning every blocking client-socket write (whole frames and injected frames, in order). Pre-WELCOME gate: nothing is read from the client socket until leg 0's WELCOME new, so the client's handshake bytes stay in the socket for a leg-0 fallback. Forward only whole frames via FrameSplitter (held-back partial bytes count as delivered for acks); keep reading client writes during an outage up to the 8 MiB cap (overflow ends the session: close client socket at a frame boundary, best-effort END{ring-overflow} on the next leg); inject LinkStatus Resuming only after the first complete downstream frame and only between frames: the first at the dead verdict (8 s silence or leg EOF), then every 1 s while resuming, Linked once after resume, never after the give-up deadline (health margin: a stall right after a client ping must not cause a health expiry, ~2 s margin); give-up deadline = grace from link loss; session-end triggers (client EOF -\u003e END best effort over the live or next leg; drop/stop; grace; overflow; unknown/ended, and new on a reconnect leg treated as session-gone); server EOF: deliver every complete frame (incl. ServerShutdown), drop a trailing partial frame, close the client socket. Leg-0 rule: after WELCOME new the session exists and retry/give-up apply; ssh-level leg-0 failure (exit 255) keeps today's semantics (no retry, failure_tx, close client socket); any remote-side failure before WELCOME (LegError::Unsupported: downgraded binary, END keeper-unavailable / server-connect-failed, non-255 exit, EOF or 8 s silence) serves that one connection via upstream plain bridge_connection with today's leg-0 options and the untouched client stream; on a reconnect leg any remote-side failure is Fatal and ends the session (outcome b), never a plain fallback mid-session. Fatal leg class (auth, host key, remote-side on a reconnect leg) -\u003e failure_tx and close the client socket at a frame boundary. With HERDR_MOSH_TRACE=\u003cdir\u003e, append JSON lines to \u003cdir\u003e/local.jsonl for leg_up, leg_down{reason}, welcome{status}, resume{replayed_up,replayed_down}, session_end{reason}, inject{state}. start_ui_bridge returns an SshStdioBridge struct literal owning the thread, should_stop and failure_tx so reported_failure() and Drop keep their semantics; plain path when kill switch, Windows remote, non-Unix local build, or no capable candidate.\nowns: LocalBridge; owns: local trace events\nconsumes: mosh constants and MoshConfig\nconsumes: start_ui_bridge; consumes: SessionEndpoint; consumes: ReplayRing; consumes: FrameSplitter; consumes: link-frame injection encoding; consumes: LegDialer; consumes: SshLegDialer; consumes: LinkStatus\nconsumes: SessionMsg (HELLO fields it sends; END reasons and their local reactions: keeper-unavailable/server-connect-failed/protocol-version → leg-0 plain fallback, server-eof → deliver then close, ring-overflow → close)\nblocked-by mosh-dqw.4: consumes SessionEndpoint\nblocked-by mosh-dqw.5: consumes FrameSplitter and encode_link_frame\nblocked-by mosh-dqw.6: consumes SshLegDialer and capability probe\nblocked-by mosh-dqw.2: consumes LinkStatus payload type\nFiles: src/mosh/local_bridge.rs, src/mosh/mod.rs\nAcceptance:\n- [ ] In-process tests with an in-memory LegDialer and fake keeper: leg killed mid-frame → client receives only whole frames, first Resuming injection at the dead verdict then every ~1 s, Linked after resume; no injection before the first frame; give-up deadline closes the client socket at a frame boundary; client writes accepted during outage; overflow (including one client message larger than 8 MiB written during an outage) ends session; Fatal → reported_failure(); leg-0 Unsupported → plain fallback.\n- [ ] Pre-WELCOME gate: no client byte is read before leg 0's WELCOME new, and the leg-0 fallback hands bridge_connection the untouched client stream; a slow client socket does not block leg reads, heartbeats, acks or should_stop polling (client-writer thread).\n- [ ] Ghost eviction: the token map is keyed by local socket path and survives a new bridge instance for the same path (saved-machine reconnect); a full reconnect sends the stored token as previous_token.\n- [ ] Health margin: a test stalls the leg immediately after a client ping and asserts no health expiry follows (first injection at the dead verdict).\n- [ ] Server EOF: complete frames (incl. ServerShutdown) delivered, trailing partial frame dropped, client socket then closed; also when the EOF arrived while the leg was down and the session then resumes.\n- [ ] Kill switch, no-capability, Windows-remote and non-Unix-local paths return the plain SshStdioBridge (platform gate unit-tested in-process).\n- [ ] Leg-0 remote-side failure (Unsupported) serves plain; leg-0 ssh-level failure (exit 255) is not retried and goes to failure_tx; any remote-side failure on a reconnect leg ends the session (Fatal, outcome b); new or unknown on a resume ends the session.\n- [ ] Input written by the client while no leg is up is buffered and delivered exactly once after resume (never dropped at the bridge); this plus server-side continuity is the whole D6 delivery mechanism (R11) — no request-level logic.\n- [ ] No upstream lines changed by this bead.\n- [ ] LinkStatus.last_contact_ms is computed from SessionEndpoint's last-inbound-time accessor.",
