+    "id": "mosh-dqw.7",
+    "title": "Keeper daemon: parked server sessions, drain and grace",
+    "description": "Remote keeper daemon (R1-R5, R7-R10, R16): parks the server connection per token across legs, drains while down, enforces grace, steals legs, evicts ghost sessions, and forwards server EOF/handoff as the remaining ring bytes then END (it never parses frames).\nSpec: docs/superpowers/runs/2026-10-24-mosh-phase1-resumable-session/2026-10-24-mosh-phase1-resumable-session-design.md (§Keeper, §Ring caps and drain policy, §Session-end triggers, §Testing Observability, §Key abstractions Keeper; Per HELLO table).\nsrc/mosh/remote/keeper.rs: keeper::run entry point (invoked by remote::dispatch for --x-mosh-keeper-v1, owned by mosh-dqw.10). Takes the \u003csocket\u003e.live lock non-blocking for its whole lifetime (exits at once if another keeper holds it), then binds the rendezvous socket path (mode 0600) defined in mosh::remote by the scaffold (mosh-dqw.1); validates the private dir via the shared helper. Spawned with null stdio and env without SSH_AUTH_SOCK by the attacher; writes diagnostics only to HERDR_MOSH_TRACE. Token table behind one lock; per session a LocalStream to client_socket_path(), a SessionEndpoint with a 16 MiB outbound ring, a server-writer thread (acks only after server writes), reads the server only when SessionEndpoint::may_read_source allows (256 KiB window with a leg up, ring cap while down), state absent/live/parked/eof, current leg, grace deadline from HELLO.grace_ms (never from the remote environment; R18). Per HELLO: previous_token applied first (ends that session if present, differs from token and names a session); v mismatch -\u003e END{protocol-version}; then the table: resume:false x absent = connect server once, create session, WELCOME new (connect failure -\u003e END{server-connect-failed}, create nothing); resume:false x live/parked/eof = END{token-in-use}, session untouched; resume:true x absent = WELCOME unknown, never opens a server connection; resume:true x live = steal leg (close the old), WELCOME resumed{recv_offset}, replay; x parked = cancel grace, resumed, replay; x eof = cancel grace, resumed, replay remaining bytes then END{server-eof}. The keeper closes the leg after any END answer. Grace timer starts when the leg drops (leg EOF or 8 s silence verdict), cancelled on resume, on expiry closes the server stream and removes the session (no tombstones). Drain policy (leg up + window full -\u003e stop reading server; leg down -\u003e keep draining into ring up to 16 MiB; overflow closes server stream, removes session). Server EOF: session enters eof; remaining ring bytes then END{server-eof} are forwarded in stream order over the live leg, or stay queued until resume/grace; removed once the local end acked the final downstream offset or at grace expiry. Idle exit is lock-ordered: once the table has been empty 30 s the keeper takes .spawn non-blocking (re-arm the timer if an attacher holds it), accepts any connection already in the listen backlog (if one exists or the table is non-empty: release .spawn, serve it, re-arm), otherwise closes the listener, unlinks the socket and exits (releasing .live then .spawn). The leg handler takes a plain duplex stream. With HERDR_MOSH_TRACE=\u003cdir\u003e, append JSON lines to \u003cdir\u003e/keeper.jsonl for welcome{status}, server_connect, leg_up, leg_down{reason}, session_end{reason}.\nowns: Keeper (fills keeper::run); owns: keeper trace events\nconsumes: mosh constants and MoshConfig\nconsumes: keeper and attacher entry-point signatures; consumes: SessionEndpoint; consumes: ReplayRing; consumes: keeper rendezvous protocol (private dir and owner checks, socket path, live lock, spawn lock)\nconsumes: SessionMsg (HELLO resume/grace_ms/previous_token fields, END reason vocabulary); consumes: rendezvous pure-pipe rule (keeper expects HELLO first, no preamble)\nblocked-by mosh-dqw.4: consumes SessionEndpoint and ReplayRing\nFiles: src/mosh/remote/keeper.rs\nAcceptance:\n- [ ] In-process tests drive a keeper against a fake server socket: every cell of the Per-HELLO table (resume:true for an absent token answers unknown with no server connection; server-connect-failed creates nothing; token-in-use leaves the session untouched; eof while parked replays the remaining bytes then END{server-eof}); protocol-version refusal; previous_token eviction; leg steal closes the old leg; the keeper closes the leg after any END; window-limited server reads with a leg up and drain-while-down captures server output; overflow ends session and the next resume is unknown; grace expiry closes server stream; server EOF forwards remaining bytes then END (no frame parsing); idle exit against a concurrent attacher (backlogged connect, held spawn lock); second keeper exits when the live lock is held.\n- [ ] No upstream lines changed by this bead.\n- [ ] The keeper never reads grace, kill switch or link thresholds from its own environment (test: remote env HERDR_MOSH_GRACE differs from HELLO.grace_ms; HELLO wins).",
