+    "id": "mosh-dqw.6",
+    "title": "SSH leg dialer: probe, re-selection, leg commands and failure classes",
+    "description": "SSH leg dialer (R1, R2, R12, R13): capability probe and candidate re-selection, leg-0 vs reconnect-leg commands (reconnect: noninteractive, ControlMaster bypassed on every leg), the leg owning its ssh child, back-off and setup deadline, and fatal/unsupported/retryable classification from structured signals.\nSpec: docs/superpowers/runs/2026-10-24-mosh-phase1-resumable-session/2026-10-24-mosh-phase1-resumable-session-design.md (§Legs, §Discovery and fallback steps 1-3, §Key abstractions Leg/LegDialer).\nsrc/mosh/ssh_leg.rs: SshLegDialer implementing LegDialer. Capability probe via remote_client_status for STATUS_CAPABILITY; candidate re-selection over remote_binary_candidates requiring the capability plus supports_endpoint_requirement (attach.rs:1519-1540,1588-1593); hint line naming HERDR_REMOTE_BINARY when none qualifies on --remote. Per-leg remote command from posix_remote_output_command + RemoteExecutable::command/session_args with [remote-client-bridge, --x-mosh-session-v1]. The leg spawns and owns its ssh child itself from a Command built with upstream builders (apply_managed_ssh_options, apply_noninteractive_ssh_options, attach.rs:1403-1440); it does NOT use bridge_child (which returns only a formatted io::Error and suppresses the exit error on client close/stop) and uses no socketpair: the child's stdin/stdout are the leg's duplex stream, the ready marker is stripped with upstream's discard_remote_output_preamble (attach.rs:3459, reachable via the #[path] mount), and the leg holds the child's ExitStatus and, on reconnect legs, its piped stderr (drained by a reader thread, capped like capture_ssh_stderr). All fork code, no upstream hook. Leg 0 uses the same ssh options as today's path (interactive inherited stderr for --remote, noninteractive for saved); no stderr is read on leg 0. Every reconnect leg is noninteractive (apply_noninteractive_ssh_options: BatchMode, ConnectTimeout=10, ConnectionAttempts=1, ServerAlive), piped stderr, and always bypasses the ControlMaster with `-o ControlPath=none -o ControlMaster=no` on the command line, with and without managed config (with managed config also a clone of ManagedSshOptions with control_path None so no -S is added, attach.rs:725-731,1421-1440). The ssh Command sets LC_ALL=C. Back-off 1,2,4,8,8… s, one leg at a time, honouring caller deadline + stop flag; a reconnect leg that does not reach HELLO within min(remaining grace, 15 s) of spawn is killed and is Retryable (leg 0 has no fork setup deadline). Classification: a leg that ended after WELCOME is always Retryable; a leg torn down for stop/session end is not classified; before WELCOME, ssh-level failure = exit status 255: on a reconnect leg Fatal if piped stderr contains 'Permission denied' or 'Host key verification failed', else Retryable; on leg 0 reported as today (failure_tx, client socket closed), no classification; remote-side failure (non-255 exit incl. 'unsupported remote client bridge option' and generation mismatch, an END from attacher/keeper before WELCOME, EOF before WELCOME, or no WELCOME within 8 s of HELLO): Unsupported on leg 0, Fatal on a reconnect leg. No stderr string is matched on leg 0.\nowns: SshLegDialer; owns: capability probe and candidate re-selection\nconsumes: mosh constants and MoshConfig\nconsumes: x-mosh-resume-bridge-v1 capability advertisement (an entry in upstream's endpoint_capabilities array of status client --json); consumes: Leg; consumes: LegDialer\nblocked-by mosh-dqw.1: consumes Leg and LegDialer interface\nFiles: src/mosh/ssh_leg.rs\nAcceptance:\n- [ ] In-process #[cfg(test)] tests (fake ssh technique of attach.rs:3684-3709): every reconnect-leg command has the noninteractive options (BatchMode, ConnectTimeout=10), `-o ControlPath=none -o ControlMaster=no`, LC_ALL=C and no -S (both managed and unmanaged config); leg-0 command equals today's; remote command contains --x-mosh-session-v1 and the session args; the leg owns its child (ExitStatus and capped stderr available, no bridge_child, no socketpair).\n- [ ] Classification tests, on leg 0 and on a reconnect leg: exit 255 with each fatal stderr string, exit 255 otherwise, non-255 exit, attacher END before WELCOME, EOF/silence before WELCOME; post-WELCOME end is Retryable; setup-deadline kill is Retryable; back-off schedule and stop/deadline honoured.\n- [ ] Probe/re-selection tests: capable first candidate; upstream-first candidate skipped for a capable later one; none capable → plain.",
