+    "description": "Whole-frame splitter and x-mosh.link.v1 injection-frame encoder (R5, R6), so the client never sees a torn frame and status frames go only between frames.\nSpec: docs/superpowers/runs/2026-10-24-mosh-phase1-resumable-session/2026-10-24-mosh-phase1-resumable-session-design.md (§Local bridge behaviour 'Whole frames'/'Injection', §Key abstractions FrameSplitter).\nsrc/mosh/link_frames.rs: FrameSplitter, an incremental u32-LE length-prefix splitter (wire.rs:1647-1715 framing) that yields whole frames, holds back partials, reports at-boundary state and rejects frames larger than MAX_GRAPHICS_FRAME_SIZE as a session-ending error, exposes the held-back partial byte count (the local bridge counts held-back bytes as delivered for acks; the hold-back is bounded by one max frame) and lets the caller drop a trailing partial frame at server EOF; used by the local bridge only (the keeper never parses frames); encode_link_frame(data_json) that produces a ServerMessage::EndpointControl{kind: LINK_KIND, data} frame via crate::protocol's existing frame writer.\nowns: FrameSplitter; owns: link-frame injection encoding\nconsumes: LinkStatus and LINK_KIND\nconsumes: mosh module tree\nblocked-by mosh-dqw.1: consumes mosh module tree\nblocked-by mosh-dqw.2: consumes LINK_KIND\nFiles: src/mosh/link_frames.rs\nAcceptance:\n- [ ] Unit tests: byte-at-a-time and random chunking reproduce the original frame sequence; partial frame held back and its length reported; trailing partial droppable; oversize rejected; an encoded link frame decodes through the real wire reader and crate::client::endpoint::decode_endpoint_control yields Ignored.",
