+  {
+    "id": "mosh-dqw.4",
+    "title": "Session protocol: SessionMsg, SessionEndpoint and ReplayRing",
+    "description": "Sans-IO session protocol (R3, R4): message codec, per-direction offsets with exactly-once dedup, the one flow-control rule (64 KiB DATA chunks, acks only after delivery, 256 KiB in-flight window while a leg is up), 2 s heartbeats and the 8 s silence verdict, resume negotiation, and the replay ring.\nSpec: docs/superpowers/runs/2026-10-24-mosh-phase1-resumable-session/2026-10-24-mosh-phase1-resumable-session-design.md (§Session wire protocol, §Ring caps and drain policy, §Key abstractions SessionMsg/SessionEndpoint/ReplayRing).\nPure, sans-IO implementation in src/mosh/session.rs and src/mosh/ring.rs: the six messages [u8 type][u32 LE len][payload] with incremental decoder; HELLO JSON {v:1, token, resume:bool, recv_offset, grace_ms, previous_token?} (resume false on the first HELLO of a session, true on every later one; no build id), WELCOME {v, status new|resumed|unknown, recv_offset}, END {reason}; DATA = [u64 LE offset][bytes] with at most 64 KiB bytes (MAX_DATA_CHUNK; larger is a leg protocol error); 128-bit Token from /dev/urandom; per-direction absolute byte offsets, dedup of overlap, gap = leg protocol error (not session). SessionEndpoint is symmetric (local end and keeper end) and owns the single flow-control rule: DATA chunking, ack-after-delivery (the owner reports delivered offsets; at the local bridge bytes in the partial-frame hold-back count as delivered; ack after \u003e=64 KiB newly delivered or 200 ms, and on every heartbeat), the fixed WINDOW = 256 KiB in-flight cap while a leg is up and the may_read_source() answer (below WINDOW while a leg is up, below the ring cap while down), window-limited replay after resume, control-before-data send ordering (pending ACK/HEARTBEAT/END precede the next DATA chunk). Timers (time passed in): 2 s HEARTBEAT while a leg is up; 8 s silence verdict, clock starting when the local end writes HELLO / the keeper reads HELLO and reset by any inbound byte including partial messages (so WELCOME must also arrive within 8 s); reconnect-leg setup deadline min(remaining grace, 15 s) from spawn, leg 0 has none. Resume negotiation: the keeper never answers new to resume:true; the local end treats new on a reconnect leg as session-gone, same as unknown; a HELLO whose v differs is refused with END{protocol-version}; replay from the peer's recv_offset. ReplayRing: bounded by caller-supplied capacity (8 MiB local, 16 MiB keeper) with push/ack-trim/replay_from/occupancy and overflow reported.\nowns: SessionMsg; owns: SessionEndpoint; owns: ReplayRing\nowns: END reason vocabulary (keeper-unavailable, server-connect-failed, protocol-version, token-in-use, server-eof, ring-overflow) and its documented required local reactions; owns: last-inbound-time accessor on SessionEndpoint (feeds LinkStatus.last_contact_ms)\nconsumes: mosh constants and MoshConfig\nconsumes: mosh module tree\nblocked-by mosh-dqw.1: consumes mosh module tree\nFiles: src/mosh/session.rs, src/mosh/ring.rs\nAcceptance:\n- [ ] Flow-control tests: DATA over 64 KiB rejected as leg error; acks advance only on delivery (received-but-queued bytes not acked); sender stops reading at WINDOW while a leg is up and keeps reading to the ring cap while down; replay after resume respects the window; control messages never queue behind more than one chunk; the silence clock starts at HELLO and resets on any byte, partial messages included; setup deadline min(remaining grace, 15 s); resume:true never yields new; new on a reconnect leg surfaces session-gone.\n- [ ] Unit tests: loss at every offset of a scripted transcript then resume delivers exactly-once in order both directions; duplicate and overlapping DATA discarded; gap rejected as leg error; double reconnect; END both directions; unknown/ended welcome surfaces resume-refused; ack cadence (64 KiB / 200 ms / heartbeat); 8 s silence verdict from injected clock.\n- [ ] Idle test (R17): two endpoints exchanging only heartbeats for \u003e8 s of injected time never reach the silence verdict; heartbeats are timer-driven, not piggybacked on data.\n- [ ] Heartbeat interval, silence timeout, MAX_DATA_CHUNK and WINDOW are compile-time constants (a change to any bumps the session-protocol version, capability string and flag together); ring caps are supplied by each end at construction; grace is carried in HELLO.grace_ms (R18).\n- [ ] Ring tests: wraparound, ack-trim, replay boundaries, occupancy, overflow reported never silent (overflow only reachable while no leg is up).\n- [ ] No sockets, threads or system clock used in these files.",
