+    "description": "Outage banner (R6): the x-mosh.link.v1 kind and LinkStatus payload, per-endpoint OutageState, and the client observe/paint hooks.\nSpec: docs/superpowers/runs/2026-10-24-mosh-phase1-resumable-session/2026-10-24-mosh-phase1-resumable-session-design.md (§Outage banner (D5), §Key abstractions LinkStatus/OutageState).\nsrc/mosh/outage.rs mounted from src/client/mod.rs as `#[path = \"../mosh/outage.rs\"] pub(crate) mod mosh_outage; // mosh-fork hook`. LINK_KIND = \"x-mosh.link.v1\" (pub(crate); fork code refers to crate::client::mosh_outage::LINK_KIND). LinkStatus serde enum tagged by \"state\": Resuming{last_contact_ms}, Linked — the single definition of the x-mosh.link.v1 payload. OutageState: process-global per-endpoint map; observe(endpoint_id, kind, data)-\u003ebool returns true only for kind x-mosh.link.v1; paint(frame, active_endpoint, label) — hook passes self.endpoint_label(\u0026self.active_endpoint_id) (client/shell/endpoints.rs:462) — draws one inverse-video top-row banner '⚠ \u003clabel\u003e unreachable — last contact \u003cN\u003es ago, resuming…' truncated to width while the active endpoint is resuming; clears on Linked and after 2 s with no status (which also covers endpoint removal/bridge teardown; no removal hook). Hook 1 at the top of the EndpointControl arm in client/mod.rs (~l.2093): a single if-statement that requests a repaint the way the arm's other UI-affecting branches do, then continue. Hook 2 in client/shell/composition.rs compose(), after the endpoint-status block and before compose_graphics (~l.719).\nowns: LinkStatus and LINK_KIND (x-mosh.link.v1); owns: OutageState\nFiles: src/mosh/outage.rs, src/client/mod.rs (2 hook lines), src/client/shell/composition.rs (1 hook line)\nAcceptance:\n- [ ] Exactly 3 upstream lines changed, each tagged // mosh-fork hook.\n- [ ] Unit tests: LinkStatus JSON round-trip with the exact field names; observe returns false for other kinds; state transitions resuming→linked clears; 2 s stale gap clears; paint writes the banner only for the active endpoint and truncates to width.\n- [ ] A frame with kind x-mosh.link.v1 never reaches decode_endpoint_control from the arm (consumed by the hook); other kinds unaffected; existing client tests pass.",
