+    "title": "Seam contract: mosh module scaffold and leg interface",
+    "description": "Inert compilable scaffold: mount line, mosh constants/MoshConfig (kill switch, grace), Leg/LegDialer/LegError, start_ui_bridge plain path with both UI call sites swapped (run_remote for --remote; connect_saved_ssh, the saved-machine supervisor connect path), and the keeper rendezvous definitions in mosh::remote (private 0700 dir with owner checks, socket path, live and spawn locks).\nSpec: docs/superpowers/runs/2026-10-24-mosh-phase1-resumable-session/2026-10-24-mosh-phase1-resumable-session-design.md (§Components, §Upstream touch list rows 1-3, §Key abstractions Leg/LegDialer/start_ui_bridge).\nCompilable scaffold that every other mosh bead fills in. Adds the single mount line in src/remote/attach.rs; creates src/mosh/mod.rs (constants STATUS_CAPABILITY=\"x-mosh-resume-bridge-v1\", flags --x-mosh-session-v1/--x-mosh-keeper-v1; env config read once: HERDR_MOSH_RESUME=0 kill switch, HERDR_MOSH_GRACE seconds default 60 clamped 5..=3600) and declares every submodule (session, ring, link_frames, ssh_leg, local_bridge, remote/{mod,attacher,keeper}) as compilable stub files; defines in ssh_leg.rs the transport-neutral Leg struct (duplex stream + teardown handle + structured end report: ExitStatus, captured stderr on reconnect legs, whether WELCOME was reached, any pre-WELCOME END reason; for ssh it owns the ssh child directly, no socketpair, no bridge_child), the LegDialer trait and LegError {Retryable, Fatal, Unsupported}; defines start_ui_bridge(ssh, remote_herdr, local_socket, session, options, noninteractive, stop) -\u003e io::Result\u003cSshStdioBridge\u003e that for now delegates to SshStdioBridge::start unchanged (inert by default; the non-Unix-local #[cfg(not(unix))] gate also lands in the plain branch), and swaps the two UI call sites (attach.rs:90 in run_remote, saved.rs:35 in connect_saved_ssh) to call it. Also defines, in src/mosh/remote/mod.rs, the single keeper rendezvous contract shared by attacher and keeper (spec §Keeper 'Rendezvous'): the private directory \u003cstd::env::temp_dir()\u003e/herdr-mosh-\u003ceuid\u003e (falling back to /tmp/herdr-mosh-\u003ceuid\u003e when the socket path would not fit sun_path, via fits_unix_socket_path), created with crate::platform::create_remote_private_dir (0700, AlreadyExists accepted) and validated before every use with symlink_metadata (a directory, not a symlink, owned by the current euid, mode exactly 0700; fork re-implementation of the private unix_common.rs check); the keeper socket \u003cdir\u003e/k-\u003ch\u003e.sock (mode 0600 when bound) where h = first 24 hex digits of SHA-256 (sha2, already a dependency) over (euid, session name, session-protocol version, build id, resolved client_socket_path()); and the sibling lock paths \u003cdir\u003e/k-\u003ch\u003e.live (keeper holds exclusive flock for its lifetime) and \u003cdir\u003e/k-\u003ch\u003e.spawn, with small helpers to take them (the attacher owns the peer-uid check itself, mosh-dqw.10). Rendezvous rule: the attacher is a pure byte pipe once connected (its only own message is END{\"keeper-unavailable\"} on bring-up failure); the session protocol starts with HELLO end to end. Stub entry points keeper::run(args) and attacher::run(args) with fixed signatures (filled by mosh-dqw.7 and mosh-dqw.10). STATUS_CAPABILITY is advertised as one entry of upstream's existing endpoint_capabilities array in `status client --json`. Creates a placeholder remote::dispatch returning None (the abstraction itself is owned by mosh-dqw.10).\nowns: mosh module tree; owns: Leg; owns: LegDialer; owns: start_ui_bridge (sole owner; mosh-dqw.8 fills its resume branch); owns: keeper rendezvous protocol (private dir and owner checks, socket path, live lock, spawn lock, pure-pipe rule; lives in mosh::remote); owns: keeper and attacher entry-point signatures; owns: mosh constants and MoshConfig\nowns: STATUS_CAPABILITY string and its placement (one entry of upstream endpoint_capabilities in status client --json); owns: --x-mosh-session-v1 / --x-mosh-keeper-v1 flag constants; owns: MoshConfig field scope (every field is local-only: the remote attacher/keeper never read grace, kill switch or thresholds from their own environment; grace reaches the keeper only via HELLO.grace_ms)\nFiles: src/remote/attach.rs (2 hook lines), src/remote/saved.rs (1), src/mosh/mod.rs, src/mosh/{session,ring,link_frames,ssh_leg,local_bridge}.rs, src/mosh/remote/{mod,attacher,keeper}.rs\nAcceptance:\n- [ ] cargo build and the full existing test suite pass; behaviour is byte-identical to upstream (start_ui_bridge always takes the plain path).\n- [ ] Exactly 3 upstream lines changed (mount + 2 swaps), each ending in // mosh-fork hook.\n- [ ] Leg, LegDialer, LegError and start_ui_bridge carry responsibility comments per the spec's Key abstractions entries.\n- [ ] Rendezvous unit tests: a foreign-owned, symlinked or wrong-mode private dir is rejected by the validation helper; the socket/lock names are stable for equal inputs and differ when client_socket_path() (or session, build id, version) differs; the path fits sun_path or falls back to /tmp.\n- [ ] Unit test: MoshConfig grace parsing clamps (unset→60, 1→5, 99999→3600, garbage→60) and kill switch.",
